#{[17592186338700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338700 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f28575a2-8621-51a3-b18b-ae5aadfa4d66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70822" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c12dba6-0a5e-5abe-ba85-6c6b625059ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338829 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70828" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31208d04-81a2-5a09-afcd-1cbba801d10f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338830 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363752 #edb/ref 1078 #