#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413460 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5979170b-e938-5576-b257-2c5e77488161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413461 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c10fc8bb-0d7f-5bee-84f8-1fa8a92dd2ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8bddb63c-4c54-5e88-a8e9-1298e5060eb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413462 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,3,5⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,2,5⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(5,-1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bced3755-fd06-539b-819f-10c4ab686823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413463 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨5,-1,1⟩$ and $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =⟨5,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(3,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fae89980-f6bf-5229-9ea3-54197530dd8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413464 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,4⟩,$ and $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
